# ── What the design was checked against ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ THE SHAPE IS THE ONE EVERY "CONNECT YOUR OWN CLUSTER" PRODUCT CONVERGED ON, and none of their code
# is here: a one-time registration token exchanged for a long-lived credential the agent keeps in a
# Secret in its own namespace; one outbound WebSocket; requests multiplexed down it by correlation id;
# a heartbeat that is what "connected" means on the platform's side. What differs from those products
# is the WIRE: this agent serves seven typed operations (TunnelOperations) rather than proxying HTTP,
# so the platform cannot send this cluster a request a reconciler could not have expressed.
#
# ⚠ THE TRANSPORT IS A WEBSOCKET AND docs/plan/09 NAMED gRPC. That section's correction carries the
# argument; the short form is that the gateway already terminates WebSockets, Directory.Packages.props
# admits no package without an ADR, and a NAT'd corporate egress that downgrades to HTTP/1.1 breaks a
# bidirectional gRPC stream and not a WebSocket.
